oad (NH-5) adjoining CGS College of Modern Technology, Vill. Khanpur, Kharar 140501, Punjab. The Complainant Deepak Sangwan has submitted that the builder is constructing G+2 floors on plot size of 72 sq.yd and 112 sq.yd and selling them as Ground, First and Second independent units. The Complainant has further submitted that the government has totally banned construction of G+2 floors on individual plots and the builder do not possess required approvals for construction of G+2 floors as per policy and has not registered in RERA. The project falls under the jurisdiction of Tehsil Kharar, which relates to the bench of vacation bench of the Authority. In terms of Order dated 10.01.2024, the powers for dealing with references/cases under Section 59, 61 and 63, have been delegated to Ld. Member (RKG), accordingly, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. Earlier, the proceedings u/s 59 of the Act has been initiated in MC00012024, accordingly, the present complaint may be tagged with the same.\r\n\r\n',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 11:40:08.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 11:40:08.000'),(410,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 11:56:36.000',1604,'MCNo00042024','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-23 11:56:37.693','','2024-02-23 11:56:37.693','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely \'Deep Residency\' located at Singh Builder and Developers, Chandigarh Ludhiana Road adjoining CGS College of Modern Technology, Vill. Khanpur, Kharar, Punjab. The Complainant Romika Jaglan has submitted that (1) the project has been launched with much fan fare and there is large scale publicity of the independent floors and flats being sold by the builder and more than 300 flats are being builtup and sold by the builder. (2) the above said builder has not got itself or the project registered under RERA Act 2016 which is in complete violation of Section 59 of RERA Act 2016. (3) the builder has also issued pamphlets for the sale of flats and is accepting money from the innocent buyers. (4) by violating the provisions of RERA Act 2016, the builder is liable to be summoned and heavy penalty be imposed. (5) the builder has not received necessary approvals in respect to pollution, mining, electrical, builders liscence, completion certificate etc. In terms of Office Order dated 10.01.2024, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. Earlier, the proceedings u/s 59 of the Act has been initiated in MC00012024, accordingly, the present complaint may be tagged with the same.\r\n\r\n\r\n',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 11:56:36.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 11:56:36.000'),(411,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:31:14.000',1603,'MCNo00032024','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-23 15:31:15.725','','2024-02-23 15:31:15.725','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely \'Deep Residency\' located at Singh Builder and Developers, Chandigarh Ludhiana Road adjoining CGS College of Modern Technology, Vill. Khanpur, Kharar, Punjab. The Complainant Sushil Kumar has submitted that (1) the project has been launched with much fan fare and there is large scale publicity of the independent floors and flats being sold by the builder and more than 300 flats are being builtup and sold by the builder. (2) the above said builder has not got itself or the project registered under RERA Act 2016 which is in complete violation of Section 59 of RERA Act 2016. (3) the builder has also issued pamphlets for the sale of flats and is accepting money from the innocent buyers. (4) by violating the provisions of RERA Act 2016, the builder is liable to be summoned and heavy penalty be imposed. (5) the builder has not received necessary approvals in respect to pollution, mining, electrical, builders liscence, completion certificate etc. In terms of Office Order dated 10.01.2024, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. Earlier, the proceedings u/s 59 of the Act has been initiated in MC00012024 filed by Shri Sushil Kumar, accordingly, the present complaint may be tagged with the same.',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:31:14.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:31:14.000'),(412,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:40:02.000',1600,'MCNo00152023','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-23 15:40:04.365','','2024-02-23 15:40:04.365','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely LANDCHESTER AERO BUSINESS PARK located at LC 2 SAS NAGAR MOHALI, Punjab. The Complainant has submitted that the promoter has accepted money via. cheque for allotment of survey deposit for commercial land in project named LC 2. the confirmation of RERA approval and further registry is awaited. The supporting documents for the same have been attached by the Complainant. In terms of office order dated 10.01.2024, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. ',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:40:02.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 15:40:02.000'),(413,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:04:28.000',1591,'MCNo00062023','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-23 16:04:29.865','','2024-02-23 16:04:29.865','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely EMERGING INDIA INFRA AND DEVOLOPERS LTD. The Complainant has submitted the complainant has booked the SP 6year\'s Plan on 09/03/2012 and paid a amount of Rs.50,000/-(Rupees Fifty thousand only) as per launch offer to the respondent out of the total cost of the flat is Rs. 109749/-(Rupees One lakh nine thousand seven hundred fourth nine only) and entered into Registration Letter. After Maturity date of agreement, the respondent refused to refund the money. This complaint has been filed under Section 18 of RERA Act against the project SP 6 year\'s plan, developed by EMERGING INDIA INFRA AND DEVOLOPERS LTD. Further, the Complainant has submitted that this project has not been registered with RERA. We may ask to the complainant to file a complaint under Section 31 of the Act of 2016 in Form M or Form N for his personal grievances and seek the report with regard to registration from the Project and Registration Branch. In terms of office order dated 10.01.2024, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. ',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:04:28.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:04:28.000'),(414,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:22:02.000',1580,'MCNo00302022','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-23 16:22:03.898','','2024-02-23 16:22:03.898','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely Greenwood Residency sector 125 Kharar. The Complainant has submitted he has not found the name of this project on RERA website so please check this unregistered project. We may seek the report in this regard from the Registration Branch of the Authority. The project falls under the jurisdiction of Tehsil Kharar, which relates to the bench of vacation bench of the Authority. In terms of Order dated 10.01.2024, the powers for dealing with references/cases under Section 59, 61 and 63, have been delegated to Ld. Member (RKG), accordingly, the complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please.',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:22:02.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-23 16:22:02.000'),(417,550048,'legaladvrera','2024-02-27 11:25:16.000',1561,'MCNo00112022','','','Authority Desk','Complaint Forwarded to Member RKG','7330c9a0-4296-4ddf-a421-0d0c491adf2d','','2024-02-27 11:25:16.584','','2024-02-27 11:25:16.584','','Present Misc. complaint has been received online under the link of \'unregistered projects complaints\'. The complaint has been received against the Project namely \'Dream City Ludhiana\' located at PLOT X103 PHASE 2C AIPL Dream City, Ludhiana, Punjab. The Complainant has submitted that IREO has abandoned this project and AIPL is now handling this property. He further submitted that his case against IREO is already under court for non fulfilment of promises as per agreement and no maintenance of the property has been done for so many years AIPL is asking for maintenance charges for this property. Bill attached. He has requested to ask AIPL to cancel the bill and stop sending further bills. As per the jurisdiction, the present complaint is forwarded to the Bench of Ld. Member (RKG) for kind consideration and further orders please. In the present matter, (i) we may advise the complainant to file a formal complaint under Section 31 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 in Form M or Form N with detailed facts mentioning the specific provisions of the RERA Act and Rules alleged to have been violated (ii) the Ld. Bench may seek the report with regard to registration of the said project from the Registration Branch of the Authority.',1,0,'legaladvrera','2024-02-27 11:25:16.000','legaladvrera','2024-02-27 11:25:16.000'),(418,550001,'999','2024